175
00:10:43,760 --> 00:10:44,590
Hello?

176
00:10:45,280 --> 00:10:47,220
Zeus, you're out! Huh?

177
00:10:47,860 --> 00:10:50,900
I don't know if I'd call
me Zeus anymore. Huh?

178
00:10:51,300 --> 00:10:55,720
I'm a cool new me after all, so why
don't you give me a cool new name?

179
00:10:57,320 --> 00:10:58,150
Uh...

180
00:10:59,220 --> 00:11:00,117
What is it?

181
00:11:00,200 --> 00:11:01,400
What is it?

182
00:11:01,620 --> 00:11:02,900
Tell me, tell me!

183
00:11:04,260 --> 00:11:05,820
Okay. Yes?

184
00:11:06,740 --> 00:11:07,720
You're a fluff!

185
00:11:12,720 --> 00:11:13,960
I'll stick with Zeus.

186
00:11:14,860 --> 00:11:18,540
If you want to get to Nami,
you gotta go through me!

187
00:11:18,820 --> 00:11:20,173
Give it your best shot!

188
00:11:22,140 --> 00:11:23,840
I'm so sick of you!

189
00:11:24,700 --> 00:11:25,980
Yeah? Same.

190
00:11:26,960 --> 00:11:28,977
We've been playing tag for long enough.

191
00:11:29,060 --> 00:11:31,700
I'm putting an end to this right now!

192
00:11:34,320 --> 00:11:35,240
Lightning!

193
00:11:48,360 --> 00:11:49,780
Oh, no!

194
00:11:50,100 --> 00:11:51,260
It's over.

195
00:11:55,620 --> 00:11:56,920
No it's not!

196
00:11:57,220 --> 00:12:01,500
It's my job to hit my target,
and that's what I'm gonna do!

197
00:12:27,820 --> 00:12:29,860
I can't believe this!

198
00:12:30,240 --> 00:12:31,820
And these are the OG!

199
00:12:33,620 --> 00:12:35,960
And with page one already done,

200
00:12:36,240 --> 00:12:40,540
they've managed to take out
two papers to tell me so slow!

201
00:12:41,740 --> 00:12:42,570
What?

202
00:12:43,460 --> 00:12:44,540
You're kidding me?

203
00:12:44,700 --> 00:12:47,037
Are these guys a lot
stronger than we thought?

204
00:12:47,120 --> 00:12:48,957
We're not actually losing, are we?

205
00:12:49,040 --> 00:12:50,040
No, we can't be!

206
00:12:50,220 --> 00:12:51,177
Calm down, miss.

207
00:12:51,260 --> 00:12:54,142
Everyone on Onigashima
can hear you freaking out!

208
00:12:54,560 --> 00:12:55,460
Oh, shoot!

209
00:12:55,760 --> 00:12:57,760
I forgot I was still broadcasting!

210
00:12:58,480 --> 00:12:59,310
Ah!

211
00:12:59,393 --> 00:13:01,340
Um, did I say, baby lady Oji?

212
00:13:01,540 --> 00:13:03,200
I meant baby Robin Lee!

213
00:13:03,740 --> 00:13:06,220
So she works as a transmitter, huh?

214
00:13:06,820 --> 00:13:08,020
All right, then.

215
00:13:08,560 --> 00:13:09,390
What?

216
00:13:09,473 --> 00:13:11,920
Special attack, green star, devil!

217
00:13:16,700 --> 00:13:18,000
Ah! What's that?

218
00:13:30,480 --> 00:13:31,700
Hey, Tama!

219
00:13:32,680 --> 00:13:36,217
I don't know how her power works,
but that girl is like a transmitter.

220
00:13:36,300 --> 00:13:39,476
If you make a command, the
whole island will hear you.

221
00:13:39,760 --> 00:13:40,860
Go for it!

222
00:14:07,080 --> 00:14:08,540
It's not a kid

223
00:14:09,820 --> 00:14:16,380
Tama is here What's she doing It's not safe
for her here It's her Go get her master

224
00:14:35,840 --> 00:14:37,760
One more round!

225
00:14:38,100 --> 00:14:39,300
One more kiss!

226
00:14:57,600 --> 00:14:59,900
It's beautiful, isn't it, Otokon?

227
00:15:02,160 --> 00:15:05,740
The fire festival is our time
to honor those we've lost.

228
00:15:06,040 --> 00:15:08,940
We build a fire to reach
them in heaven itself.

229
00:15:09,940 --> 00:15:12,440
I wonder if Daddy can see it.

230
00:15:14,340 --> 00:15:16,400
Yes, of course he can.

231
00:15:16,820 --> 00:15:19,480
There isn't a cloud in the sky, after all.

232
00:15:22,000 --> 00:15:24,957
I'm sure he's watching
over you and watching

233
00:15:25,040 --> 00:15:27,940
over the fate of this
country he loved so well.

234
00:15:41,960 --> 00:15:43,700
you heard a voice

235
00:15:48,140 --> 00:15:53,640
someone's there what you're right i see
something wait a sec is that Straw Hat

236
00:15:54,480 --> 00:15:56,817
How the hell did you hear him underwater?

237
00:15:56,900 --> 00:15:58,680
Who cares? Just bring him in!

238
00:16:00,080 --> 00:16:00,910
Hurry!

239
00:16:00,993 --> 00:16:01,823
He might be alive!

240
00:16:02,440 --> 00:16:04,180
Whose baby is that?

241
00:16:04,420 --> 00:16:06,361
Get out of here, you little shit!

242
00:16:06,560 --> 00:16:07,854
This is a battlefield!

243
00:16:08,280 --> 00:16:10,751
And what the hell did you do to Bao Huang?

244
00:16:11,760 --> 00:16:12,720
Answer me!

245
00:16:16,700 --> 00:16:17,530
Tama!

246
00:16:17,613 --> 00:16:18,443
Hang in there!

247
00:16:18,560 --> 00:16:19,400
You got this!

248
00:16:35,980 --> 00:16:38,417
Aren't you going to complain
about being outnumbered?

249
00:16:38,500 --> 00:16:39,676
Seems pretty unfair.

250
00:16:39,940 --> 00:16:42,800
It was 5,000 versus
30,000 when we came here.

251
00:16:43,060 --> 00:16:46,137
This is what everyone expected
from the very beginning.

252
00:16:46,220 --> 00:16:49,220
A one-on-one battle was
never in the cards for me.

253
00:16:49,440 --> 00:16:51,520
How annoyingly pragmatic of you.

254
00:16:51,840 --> 00:16:53,197
This is no fun.

255
00:16:53,280 --> 00:16:56,680
Our job is to keep the top
officers busy till Luffy wins,

256
00:16:56,880 --> 00:16:58,704
so grumble as long as you like.

257
00:17:01,020 --> 00:17:03,700
It's one after another with these guys.

258
00:17:05,480 --> 00:17:08,900
A knock them down, and more show up.

259
00:17:10,780 --> 00:17:13,360
Strength and determination mean nothing.

260
00:17:14,540 --> 00:17:16,800
No matter what matters in this game.

261
00:17:17,960 --> 00:17:21,820
Because this isn't a
battle, it's an Alto war.

262
00:17:23,280 --> 00:17:25,456
It's your own fault for getting that.

263
00:17:29,100 --> 00:17:32,060
What the hell is she still doing up there?

264
00:17:32,320 --> 00:17:34,460
Just looking at her pisses me off.

265
00:17:34,600 --> 00:17:36,718
Hey, someone take care of that brat.

266
00:17:37,020 --> 00:17:38,360
Right, on it, sir.

267
00:17:38,640 --> 00:17:40,100
Let's go. Yeah.

268
00:17:40,440 --> 00:17:42,780
Tama, hurry. Wait, now.

269
00:17:43,820 --> 00:17:47,300
Hey, all of my friends do STB Tang.

270
00:17:47,680 --> 00:17:50,460
I need to ask you a favor.

271
00:17:51,120 --> 00:17:53,240
Can you switch sides, please?

272
00:17:53,740 --> 00:17:56,660
Big bro, Lumi, and Mama
Natsuka, do you do?

273
00:17:56,880 --> 00:17:58,620
You've got to have some fun!

274
00:18:03,480 --> 00:18:07,520
Let's all work together
and turn down Carter!

275
00:18:16,440 --> 00:18:18,017
The hell was that?

276
00:18:18,100 --> 00:18:22,660
You think they'll listen to you just
because you ass nice, you dumb brat?

277
00:18:23,060 --> 00:18:26,040
You're gonna pay for
putting it on my show!

278
00:18:30,240 --> 00:18:31,520
Roger that, Master!

279
00:18:31,880 --> 00:18:33,292
Your wish is my command!

280
00:18:33,500 --> 00:18:34,760
Take down Tidal!

281
00:18:35,340 --> 00:18:36,960
Now, let's start with you!

282
00:18:39,060 --> 00:18:40,540
Get off of me!

283
00:18:40,800 --> 00:18:42,682
What the hell is wrong with you?

284
00:18:44,380 --> 00:18:46,717
What's wrong, General Briscola? Let's go!

285
00:18:46,800 --> 00:18:51,035
Well, we're here to take out some
traitors, so let's stomp them already.

286
00:18:51,140 --> 00:18:54,260
All right, I heard you
loud and clear, Master.

287
00:18:54,940 --> 00:18:58,764
Let's start out with a Gorilla
Punch-Punch, just for you, Master.

288
00:18:59,660 --> 00:19:02,425
All right, looks like
Master's given the order.

289
00:19:03,520 --> 00:19:07,600
Gazelle Man, Daifugo, it's
time to join the fight. Yeah!

290
00:19:09,580 --> 00:19:11,040
You see that, Master?

291
00:19:11,280 --> 00:19:12,420
I'm working hard.

292
00:19:12,700 --> 00:19:14,717
Why are all the dipters trying to kill us?

293
00:19:14,800 --> 00:19:15,630
I don't know, man.

294
00:19:15,713 --> 00:19:16,580
Just run away!

295
00:19:17,940 --> 00:19:19,760
We're coming for you, Kaido!

296
00:19:20,080 --> 00:19:21,160
Let's do this!

297
00:19:23,200 --> 00:19:25,120
Everyone follow me!

298
00:19:30,620 --> 00:19:32,540
Gifters, lend me your strength!

299
00:19:32,780 --> 00:19:36,074
Let's fight for our wonderful
master with all we've got!

300
00:19:49,680 --> 00:19:50,660
You're the best!

301
00:19:50,900 --> 00:19:51,860
Thank you, guys!

302
00:19:57,980 --> 00:19:58,900
No, Bryce!

303
00:19:59,000 --> 00:20:00,000
He's all floated!

304
00:20:00,220 --> 00:20:01,457
I told you he was dead.

305
00:20:01,540 --> 00:20:03,069
And I told you to shut up!

306
00:20:03,180 --> 00:20:04,517
You're not helping at all!

307
00:20:04,600 --> 00:20:05,430
What do we do?

308
00:20:05,513 --> 00:20:07,912
Captain can help if you were here, but...

309
00:20:08,860 --> 00:20:09,720
Stop fighting.

310
00:20:09,900 --> 00:20:11,488
We need to clear his lungs.

311
00:20:12,160 --> 00:20:14,180
One, two, three!

312
00:20:19,200 --> 00:20:20,030
Boobside!

313
00:20:34,080 --> 00:20:36,757
Well, if he wasn't dead, you
might have just killed him.

314
00:20:36,840 --> 00:20:38,428
He's rubber, he'll be fine.

315
00:20:39,120 --> 00:20:41,000
Well, I hope he will at least.

316
00:20:44,760 --> 00:20:45,590
Okay.

317
00:20:46,120 --> 00:20:47,540
It's not okay!

318
00:20:48,000 --> 00:20:49,520
God, that rubber's burnt.

319
00:20:49,640 --> 00:20:51,000
Captain, help us!

320
00:20:57,440 --> 00:21:00,080
He missed you! He missed you!

321
00:21:00,300 --> 00:21:01,359
He missed you too!

322
00:21:02,860 --> 00:21:05,940
But like kites, we rise
highest against the wind!

323
00:21:08,020 --> 00:21:09,820
Neempo, great kite!

324
00:21:16,900 --> 00:21:17,730
Excellent.

325
00:21:18,080 --> 00:21:20,880
Now if I can just find a place to land.

326
00:21:27,040 --> 00:21:28,557
That was awful.

327
00:21:28,640 --> 00:21:32,840
We escaped from that horrible
place, but what costs?

328
00:21:33,300 --> 00:21:35,220
What happened to the others?

329
00:21:35,680 --> 00:21:38,300
Do you think they could still be alive?

330
00:21:44,340 --> 00:21:45,740
KIKU!

331
00:21:45,920 --> 00:21:47,057
KINEMAN!

332
00:21:47,140 --> 00:21:48,540
EVERYONE!

333
00:22:03,500 --> 00:22:04,900
Candy!

334
00:22:13,360 --> 00:22:16,600
I think you mean father,
don't you, Yamato?

335
00:22:17,260 --> 00:22:19,820
I'm here to finally cut ties with you!

336
00:22:20,880 --> 00:22:21,710
Hmm.

337
00:22:23,320 --> 00:22:25,960
Are you sure about that, son?

338
00:22:39,960 --> 00:22:41,677
Don't make me laugh.

339
00:22:41,760 --> 00:22:43,960
You have nothing without me.

340
00:22:44,900 --> 00:22:47,080
Straw Hat is sunk into the sea.

341
00:22:49,260 --> 00:22:51,700
Odin's son suffered the same fate.

342
00:22:53,740 --> 00:22:55,620
If you have the will to fight,

343
00:22:55,860 --> 00:22:58,657
you should have protected
them while you had the chance.

344
00:22:58,740 --> 00:22:59,877
You've got it wrong.

345
00:22:59,960 --> 00:23:01,417
I don't need to protect them.

346
00:23:01,500 --> 00:23:03,437
They're both much stronger than you think.

347
00:23:03,520 --> 00:23:07,120
I fight beside them, as equals.

348
00:23:07,940 --> 00:23:09,740
And what happens after that?

349
00:23:10,500 --> 00:23:13,097
You think you're gonna
break free of this country?

350
00:23:13,180 --> 00:23:14,010
Of me?

351
00:23:14,460 --> 00:23:15,380
I am.

352
00:23:15,640 --> 00:23:18,257
Luffy will show me the
world you've kept from me.

353
00:23:18,340 --> 00:23:21,677
But before I leave here, I'm
kicking you out of this country.

354
00:23:21,760 --> 00:23:22,590
Understand?

355
00:23:34,620 --> 00:23:37,300
I won't be going anywhere.

356
00:23:40,320 --> 00:23:42,720
The land of water is extraordinary.

357
00:23:43,260 --> 00:23:45,280
There's no place like it.

358
00:23:46,460 --> 00:23:50,100
You can't defeat me, and I'll never leave.

359
00:23:51,460 --> 00:23:55,200
So stay with me, and become
the Shogun of this country!

360
00:23:57,260 --> 00:23:58,840
I told you no!

361
00:23:59,260 --> 00:24:01,848
And I know I won't be
the one to defeat you.

362
00:24:01,940 --> 00:24:02,860
That's Luffy!

363
00:24:03,520 --> 00:24:06,760
Because he's the man Kozuki
Oden was waiting for!

364
00:24:09,140 --> 00:24:11,660
He'll return stronger than ever!

365
00:24:12,020 --> 00:24:14,720
All I have to do is
keep you busy till then.

366
00:24:16,380 --> 00:24:19,760
Don't expect me to go easy on you, Yamato.

367
00:24:22,500 --> 00:24:23,900
No mercy!

368
00:24:29,680 --> 00:24:31,120
No mercy!
